cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite the paper (preferred citation)
  and this repository. When using the REMIND results, please also cite
  REMIND v3.6.0.
type: software
title: "ecemf-wp1-mip-paper: data and code for 'Milestones to Net Zero: Intermodel insights on the EU's 2040 climate targets'"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository to the ECEMF Work Package 1 model intercomparison
  paper. It contains the scenario results of ten energy-system and integrated
  assessment models (from the IIASA ECEMF Scenario Explorer), historical
  reference data, and the R code that computes all numbers quoted in the
  manuscript and draws all figures.
